# Build-time hooks, NN-name executables, run in lexical order by
# saphira-mkinitramfs while it CONSTRUCTS an archive.
#
# These are NOT shipped in the initramfs and do NOT run at boot. They run on
# the BUILDING system, from a package that may legitimately depend on
# compilers and other build-time software. Runtime hooks, which are shipped
# and executed by /init, live under /lib/saphira/initramfs/ and are named in
# the configuration instead.
#
# The distinction is a directory boundary on purpose. One directory doing both
# jobs would mean an initramfs could end up depending, at boot, on software
# that only exists because a build happened to need it.
#
# Environment provided to every hook:
#
#   SAPHIRA_INITRAMFS_STAGE    staging tree being assembled; add files here
#   SAPHIRA_INITRAMFS_ROOT     the root the payload is collected from
#   SAPHIRA_INITRAMFS_KERNEL   the --kernel value
#   SAPHIRA_INITRAMFS_CONFIG   the configuration file in use
#
# Whatever a hook adds to the stage is normalised for ownership, modes and
# timestamps along with everything else, so a hook does not need to care.
#
# A non-zero exit fails the build. The previous initramfs is never touched by
# a failed build.
#
# No hooks ship in this package: the base initramfs needs none.
